  "Question": "If \\(a-1=b+2=c-3=d+4,\\) which of the four quantities \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c,\\) \\(d\\) is the largest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a\\)",
    "B": "\\(b\\)",
    "C": "\\(c\\)",
    "D": "\\(d\\)",
    "E": "no one is always largest"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Let \\(t\\) be the common value of the four equal expressions. Solving each equality for its letter gives\n\\[\na=t+1,\\qquad b=t-2,\\qquad c=t+3,\\qquad d=t-4.\n\\]\nAdding the same number \\(t\\) preserves order. Since \\(-4<-2<1<3\\), we have \\(d<b<a<c\\) for every possible \\(t\\). Thus \\(\\boxed{c}\\) is always largest, choice C.",
